type: dataset
title: "Japan transformer-level hourly loading and capacity tables: harmonized derived dataset"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-20"
authors:
  - family-names: Jing
    given-names: Jiawei
repository-code: "https://github.com/ibarapascal/japan-substation-headroom"
url: "https://github.com/ibarapascal/japan-substation-headroom"
# Data and documentation: CC BY 4.0 (LICENSE-DATA). Code: MIT (LICENSE).
license: CC-BY-4.0
abstract: >-
  Harmonized tables derived from two disclosures published by each of Japan's ten
  general transmission and distribution operators: hourly measured power flow on the
  secondary side of substation transformers, and transformer capacity tables (number of
  units, rated capacity, operating capacity, forecast flow, published available capacity).
  The code downloads the published files, parses the operator-specific layouts into one
  hourly long table and one capacity table, computes substation-year statistics of the
  coincident hourly load (annual peak, percentiles, zero and negative hours), joins them to
  the capacity tables by normalized substation name and voltage, and reports load-direction
  headroom under two definitions (operating capacity minus annual peak; (units-1)/units of
  rated capacity minus annual peak). The dataset also contains the TEPCO Power Grid
  per-area capacity lists of 2019-2025 parsed from Internet Archive copies, a register of
  data center sites in Japan built from facility-level emission reports (EEGS) and public
  announcements, and factual items coded from the operators' voluntary demand-side siting
  guides with a per-operator inventory of grid disclosure items. Source files are not
  redistributed; a manifest records their URLs and SHA-256 checksums. Code is licensed
  under MIT and data files under CC BY 4.0.
keywords:
  - electricity distribution
  - substation
  - transformer loading
  - hosting capacity
  - data center
  - Japan
